1. Scope

This license applies to every file in the `packages/ee/` directory of this
repository and to any file whose header carries the identifier
`LicenseRef-DMS-Commercial` (together, the "Commercial Software"). It has
applied to the Commercial Software from its first commit. The Commercial
Software has never been, and is not, licensed under the GNU Affero General
Public License that covers the rest of this repository.

2. Production use requires a valid license key

You may use the Commercial Software in production only while you hold a valid
license key issued by the licensor for the deployment, and only within the
features, locations and term that the key grants. A license key is valid when
its signature verifies against the licensor's published public key, it has not
expired, and it was issued for your dealer or installation.

3. Launch promotion

The licensor may publish a free promotion license key. The promotion key is a
valid license key under section 2 until the expiry date published with it. No
payment, payment card or automatic conversion to a paid plan is required to
use it. The licensor will announce the end of the promotion, and any change to
which features are free, publicly at least 90 days in advance (repository
notice and in-app notice).

4. Development and testing

Without a license key you may copy, modify and run the Commercial Software for
development, testing and evaluation, provided you do not use it to process
real customer data or real dealer business.

5. After a key ends

When a license key or the promotion ends, the Commercial Software stops
allowing new or changed data in paid features. Data you created with paid
features stays readable and exportable. Loan payment posting for in-house
financing (BHPH) loans written while a valid key (including the promotion key)
was in force stays available for the life of those loans.

6. Restrictions

Except as allowed above, you may not: (a) sell, sublicense, or distribute the
Commercial Software or modified versions of it; (b) remove, bypass or disable
the license-key check or any feature gate; or (c) remove this license or the
copyright notices.

